From 8a3024857f07cc2b276712a47828d6b3b6a1c45b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:45:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PM P2: FADT, DSDT and GPE0 (PM_PLAN P2)

The kernel lane can now find PM: acpi.c grows a revision-4
FADT (field offsets taken from the ACPICA definition) and a
DSDT whose only object is \_S5 = Package(7,0) -- the exact
sleep type P1 decodes, pinned byte-for-byte by the vector.
The FADT advertises exactly what pm.c implements: SCI on
IRQ9, PM1a EVT/CNT/TMR and GPE0 at PM_DEFAULT_BASE with
agreeing 64-bit GAS mirrors, block lengths 4/2/4/8,
SMI_CMD=0 (no SMM exists here), 24-bit timer, RESET_REG at
the 0xCF9 port the chipset decodes with value 0x0E. RSDT
and XSDT list FACP then APIC; the old one-pointer vectors
were updated to the new contract and the tamper loop now
covers all five tables.

GPE0 joins the block: STS W1C and EN stored at +0x20/+0x24,
added to the level-SCI expression. No GPE sources exist yet
-- the vector pokes the latch directly to prove the wire;
sources arrive with their consumers.

NC: pm.c+acpi.c reverted to P1 under the P2 header -- both
suites abort behaviourally (GPE0_EN store; RSDT length).
Gates: make test + sanitize green; both SeaBIOS ISO lanes
green with the stock bios.bin present (P1's gate had run in
skip mode -- recorded in the plan). The S1 fork is measured
for P3 (no consumer needs real parking; zero-duration is
spec-legal) in PM_PLAN.md 2c. Docs: PM_PLAN.md (P2 receipts,
D3/D4 resolved), STATUS.md, CHANGELOG.md.
